2. The following offences may be compounded by the Director in accordance with section 69(1) of the Act:
(a)any offence under section 8(6), 14(14), 15(2), 16(11), 20(8), 25(5), 29(3), 34(4) or 49(6) of the Act;
(b)any offence under the Merchant Shipping (Maritime Labour Convention) (Wages) Regulations 2014 (G.N. No. S 174/2014);
(c)any offence under the Merchant Shipping (Maritime Labour Convention) (Health and Safety Protection and Accident Prevention) Regulations 2014 (G.N. No. S 177/2014);
(d)any offence under the Merchant Shipping (Maritime Labour Convention) (Seafarer Recruitment and Placement Services) Regulations 2014 (G.N. No. S 178/2014);
(e)any offence under the Merchant Shipping (Maritime Labour Convention) (Medicines and Medical Equipment) Regulations 2014 (G.N. No. S 181/2014); and
(f)any offence under the Merchant Shipping (Maritime Labour Convention) (Repatriation) Regulations 2014 (G.N. No. S 208/2014).
